    "HELD_NON_ACTIVE_ENDPOINT",
    "HELD_INTEGRITY_GAP"
  ],
  "lifecycle_rules": [
    "A registered edge whose asserted relationship conflicts with its current source fields must be HELD_INTEGRITY_GAP pending W3 reconciliation.",
    "An edge touching a DRAFT, HELD, RETIRED, or W1-held graph node must be HELD_NON_ACTIVE_ENDPOINT.",
    "An explicit block, confirmation, targeting, fact-only, or internal-projection edge, an edge governed by an internal-only policy, or an edge touching a never-external endpoint must be INTERNAL_TRAVERSAL_ONLY unless held.",
    "Only ACTIVE_POLICY_GATED edges may enter a future release-authorizing cluster after all later-wave gates pass.",
    "A hardened edge never promotes an ineligible endpoint."
  ],
